 2047-08-15, 2047-11-01, 2047-11-11, 2047-12-24, 2047-12-25, 2047-12-26, 2048-01-01, 2048-01-06, 2048-04-05, 2048-04-06, 2048-05-01, 2048-05-03, 2048-05-24, 2048-06-04, 2048-08-15, 2048-11-01, 2048-11-11, 2048-12-24, 2048-12-25, 2048-12-26, 2049-01-01, 2049-01-06, 2049-04-18, 2049-04-19, 2049-05-01, 2049-05-03, 2049-06-06, 2049-06-17, 2049-08-15, 2049-11-01, 2049-11-11, 2049-12-24, 2049-12-25, 2049-12-26, 2050-01-01, 2050-01-06, 2050-04-10, 2050-04-11, 2050-05-01, 2050-05-03, 2050-05-29, 2050-06-09, 2050-08-15, 2050-11-01, 2050-11-11, 2050-12-24, 2050-12-25, 2050-12-26, 2051-01-01, 2051-01-06, 2051-04-02, 2051-04-03, 2051-05-01, 2051-05-03, 2051-05-21, 2051-06-01, 2051-08-15, 2051-11-01, 2051-11-11, 2051-12-24, 2051-12-25, 2051-12-26, 2052-01-01, 2052-01-06, 2052-04-21, 2052-04-22, 2052-05-01, 2052-05-03, 2052-06-09, 2052-06-20, 2052-08-15, 2052-11-01, 2052-11-11, 2052-12-24, 2052-12-25, 2052-12-26, 2053-01-01, 2053-01-06, 2053-04-06, 2053-04-07, 2053-05-01, 2053-05-03, 2053-05-25, 2053-06-05, 2053-08-15, 2053-11-01, 2053-11-11, 2053-12-24, 2053-12-25, 2053-12-26, 2054-01-01, 2054-01-06, 2054-03-29, 2054-03-30, 2054-05-01, 2054-05-03, 2054-05-17, 2054-05-28, 2054-08-15, 2054-11-01, 2054-11-11, 2054-12-24, 2054-12-25, 2054-12-26, 2055-01-01, 2055-01-06, 2055-04-18, 2055-04-19, 2055-05-01, 2055-05-03, 2055-06-06, 2055-06-17, 2055-08-15, 2055-11-01, 2055-11-11, 2055-12-24, 2055-12-25, 2055-12-26, 2056-01-01, 2056-01-06, 2056-04-02, 2056-04-03, 2056-05-01, 2056-05-03, 2056-05-21, 2056-06-01, 2056-08-15, 2056-11-01, 2056-11-11, 2056-12-24, 2056-12-25, 2056-12-26, 2057-01-01, 2057-01-06, 2057-04-22, 2057-04-23, 2057-05-01, 2057-05-03, 2057-06-10, 2057-06-21, 2057-08-15, 2057-11-01, 2057-11-11, 2057-12-24, 2057-12-25, 2057-12-26]) "calendar.ts holidays(y) for 2024 to 2057, Easter by the anonymous Gregorian algorithm"
,16:r7/forward.tally,13039:part r7_forward
  tally 2
  note "T, M2 (issues #167, #114), DONE gate 2: the forward half of the prototype's reality R7 (load.ts REALITY: blocks 01-month, 03-ike-first, 04-employment, 05-side-business, 07-oki; engine/spec/verification/goldens.md: G1, G3, G6, G10 and the 20 pins), beside the bank half (../bank.tally), from today, 2026-10-17. Here: the daily spending (01), the 15th rule with IKE first (02, 03, 07), the ETF units and their price (01), OKI's tax (07), net worth and FIRE (13). The side business is business.tally, the yearly returns returns.tally; the header (to2036.tally, to2050.tally, to2056.tally) states the horizon."
  note "The holdings: the prototype converts each movement into a holding at that day's price.etf (run.ts post: units = amount / price), and price.etf changes only on the 1st of a month. So the PLN the bank history moves into ike and maklerskie (accounts here, as the records state them) is bought at the month's last day at that month's price (buy_ike, buy_mak), which gives the prototype's units, and the 15th rule buys its units on its day. Units are kept to units_step and each month's price to etf_price_step (the prototype keeps floats); price.etf from 2026-11 is the month before's times pow(1.06, 1 / 12), stated as the factor."
  note "The 15th rule (nadwyzka_ike@1, instances invest_15 and from 2027 invest_15_oki): surplus = max(0, low_point(konto, next_date(my_tax/net)) - floor), the lowest end-of-day konto from the rule's day to the day before my next pay, the rule's own buy left out (L §5.14.1); to IKE min(surplus, max(0, ike.limit - in_year(ike))), the rest to maklerskie, and from 2027 to OKI. One move takes both, as the prototype computes the surplus once. The prototype runs it from today on: invest_from."
  note "Not stated: belka_mak (03), the 19 % tax on gains realised on maklerskie, which nothing sells, so its tax is 0 every year; the side business's social contributions, 0 in concurrence (business.tally)."

source prototype_fwd "the prototype's blocks 01-month.json, 02-rule-15.json, 03-ike-first.json, 07-oki.json and 13-fire.json, and its engine (run.ts) (engine/spec/verification/blocks)"

source rpp "Komunikaty Rady Polityki Pieniężnej o stopach procentowych NBP (07-oki.json nbp.ref_rate)"

source oki_act "Ustawa o osobistych kontach inwestycyjnych, Dz.U. 2026 poz. 1098 (07-oki.json, z prototypu)"

source ike_act "Ustawa o IKE art. 13 (03-ike-first.json ike.limit)"

unit etf_unit "jednostka funduszu ETF na świat"

kind etf_buys: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  leg units: etf_unit

kind rule15_buys: event certain
  leg to_ike: PLN
  leg ike_units: etf_unit
  leg to_mak: PLN
  leg mak_units: etf_unit
  leg to_oki: PLN
  leg oki_units: etf_unit

place ike_u: holdings etf_unit lives 2024-01-01..

place mak_u: holdings etf_unit lives 2024-01-01..

place oki_u: holdings etf_unit lives 2024-01-01..

place rynek: outside lives 2024-01-01..

input etf_from: month

input etf_month_factor: num

input etf_price_step: num PLN/etf_unit

input etf_seen: num PLN/etf_unit

input fire_from: month

input fire_rate: num

input floor_15: money PLN

input ike_limit: money PLN

input invest_dom: int

input invest_from: month

input nbp_months: int

input nbp_ref: num

input oki_exempt: money PLN

input oki_from: month

input oki_rate_first: num

input oki_rate_floor: num

input oki_rate_step: num

input oki_ref_from: date

input oki_ref_share: num

input oki_tax_day: int

input oki_tax_month: int

input units_step: num etf_unit

def etf_price[m in month]: num PLN/etf_unit at start_of(m)
  note "01-month.json price.etf: the synthetic history to 2026-10, then before * pow(1 + assume.etf_return, 1 / 12) each month from 2026-11-01: before times the month's factor, the float the prototype multiplies by, each month's price kept to etf_price_step (the prototype's floats keep about 16 digits)"
  rule seen = etf_seen
  rule assumed beats seen = round(etf_price[m - 1] * etf_month_factor, etf_price_step, half-even) when m >= etf_from

def spend_rate: num PLN at learn_last
  note "01-month.json wydatki@1: hist_daily(codzienne, 365), the sum of the last 365 days' codzienne rows / 365, not rounded (run.ts hist_daily)"
  rule learned = sum(o.cash.amount for o in bank_line over learn_first .. learn_last where o.cat == codzienne) / (days_between(learn_first, learn_last) + 1) when covered(konto, learn_first .. learn_last)

def spend_amount[y in cal_year]: money PLN = round(spend_rate * price_index[y], minor(PLN), half-up) at start_of(y)
  note "a day's spending, hist_daily * index.prices, to the grosz as run.ts books every movement"

def next_pay[m in month]: date = pay_day[my_job, m] at start_of(m)
  note "next_date(my_tax/net) on the 15th of m: the pay for m, on the 3rd to 7th of the next month (the pay for m - 1 falls before the 15th)"

def surplus[m in month]: money PLN = max(0, low(konto, day_of(m, invest_dom) .. add_days(next_pay[m], -1)) from day_of(m, invest_dom) - floor_15) at start_of(m)
  note "nadwyzka_ike@1 surplus: max(0, low_point(in.from, next_date(in.until)) - in.floor)"

def ike_seen[y in cal_year]: money PLN at start_of(y)
  note "in_year(ike) from the bank history: the year's rows into ike up to the last day of the history"
  rule history = sum(o.cash.amount for o in bank_line over start_of(y) .. learn_last where o.cash.to == ike) when start_of(y) <= learn_last
  rule after beats history = 0 when start_of(y) > learn_last

def ike_in[m in month]: money PLN = ike_seen[year_of(m)] + flows(invest.to_ike, start_of(year_of(m)) .. add_days(day_of(m, invest_dom), -1)) at start_of(m)
  note "in_year(ike): what went into the IKE this year before the rule's day"

def to_ike[m in month]: money PLN = min(surplus[m], max(0, ike_limit - ike_in[m])) at start_of(m)
  note "nadwyzka_ike@1 to_ike: min(v('surplus'), max(0, p.ike.limit - in_year(in.ike)))"

def rest[m in month]: money PLN = surplus[m] - to_ike[m] at start_of(m)
  note "nadwyzka_ike@1 to_rest: v('surplus') - v('to_ike'), to maklerskie (invest_15) and from 2027 to OKI (invest_15_oki)"

def oki_rate[y in cal_year]: num at start_of(y)
  note "07-oki.json oki.rate: 0.85 % in 2027, then 19 % of the NBP reference rate of 31 October before, down to 0.01 pp, at least 0.1 %"
  rule first = oki_rate_first
  rule by_ref beats first = max(oki_rate_floor, round(oki_ref_share * nbp_ref_oct[y], oki_rate_step, floor)) when start_of(y) >= oki_ref_from

def nbp_ref_oct[y in cal_year]: num = nbp_ref at add_months(add_days(start_of(y), -1), -nbp_months)
  note "the NBP reference rate on 31 October of the year before"

def oki_avg[y in cal_year]: num PLN = sum(value(oki_u, d) in PLN by etf_price[month_of(d)] for d in start_of(y) .. add_days(end_of(y), -1) step 1 day) / days_between(start_of(y), end_of(y)) at start_of(y)
  note "oki_pl@2027 avg: avg_balance(in.oki), the mean end-of-day value over the year's days (OKI from 2027-01-01)"

def oki_tax[y in cal_year]: money PLN = round(max(0, oki_avg[y] - oki_exempt) * oki_rate[y], 1, half-up) at start_of(y)
  note "oki_pl@2027 tax: zl(max(0, v('avg') - v('exempt')) * p.oki.rate), holds foreign: no exempt amount"

def net_worth[d in day]: money PLN = round(bal(konto, d) + bal(ike, d) + bal(maklerskie, d) + value(ike_u, d) in PLN by etf_price[month_of(d)] + value(mak_u, d) in PLN by etf_price[month_of(d)] + value(oki_u, d) in PLN by etf_price[month_of(d)], minor(PLN), half-up) at d
  note "run.ts networthAt: every place that isn't outside, a holding at units * price (the household's places, all its own; M1's P7)"

def fire_costs[m in month]: num PLN = spend_rate * price_index[year_of(m)] * days_between(start_of(m), end_of(m)) + rent * price_index[year_of(m)] at start_of(m)
  note "fire@1 costs: total('spend', spending) + v('rent', housing), the lines' values before rounding (run.ts stores them so)"

def fire_on_track[m in month]: bool = net_worth[add_days(end_of(m), -1)] >= fire_costs[m] * (1 year / 1 month) / fire_rate at start_of(m)
  note "fire@1 on_track: have >= need, have at the month's end, need = costs * 12 / p.assume.fire_swr"

move buy_ike[m in month]: etf_buys
  on add_days(end_of(m), -1)
  at start_of(m)
  when m < invest_from
  reads ike
  leg cash from ike to rynek amount bal(ike)
  leg units from rynek to ike_u amount round(bal(ike) / etf_price[m], units_step, half-even)

move buy_mak[m in month]: etf_buys
  on add_days(end_of(m), -1)
  at start_of(m)
  when m < invest_from
  reads maklerskie
  leg cash from maklerskie to rynek amount bal(maklerskie)
  leg units from rynek to mak_u amount round(bal(maklerskie) / etf_price[m], units_step, half-even)

move invest[m in month]: rule15_buys
  on day_of(m, invest_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  when m >= invest_from
  reads konto, invest
  leg to_ike from konto to rynek amount to_ike[m]
  leg ike_units from rynek to ike_u amount round(to_ike[m] / etf_price[m], units_step, half-even)
  leg to_mak from konto to rynek amount if m < oki_from then rest[m] else 0 PLN
  leg mak_units from rynek to mak_u amount if m < oki_from then round(rest[m] / etf_price[m], units_step, half-even) else 0 etf_unit
  leg to_oki from konto to rynek amount if m >= oki_from then rest[m] else 0 PLN
  leg oki_units from rynek to oki_u amount if m >= oki_from then round(rest[m] / etf_price[m], units_step, half-even) else 0 etf_unit

move oki_tax_pay[y in cal_year]: transfers
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(add_years(start_of(y), 1), oki_tax_month - 1)), oki_tax_day, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(y)
  for y
  when start_of(y) >= start_of(oki_from)
  reads oki_u
  leg cash from konto to urzad_skarbowy amount oki_tax[y]

move spend[d in day]: transfers
  on d
  at d
  leg cash from konto to sklepy amount spend_amount[year_of(d)]

version prototype_assumptions
  cite prototype_fwd
  governs always
  known 2026-10-17
  inflation = 0.03 governs 2027-01-01.. "01-month.json assume.inflation: 3 % a year from 2027-01-01 (NBP target 2.5 % ± 1)"
  wage_growth = 0.04 governs 2027-01-01.. "01-month.json assume.wage_growth: 4 % a year from 2027-01-01"
  etf_month_factor = 1.004867550565343 "01-month.json assume.etf_return, 6 % a year from 2026-10-17, as price.etf applies it each month: pow(1 + 0.06, 1 / 12), the float the prototype multiplies by"

version prototype_rules
  cite prototype_fwd
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  note "the prototype's fixture is one model with one today: its price history, its rule and its plan are stated for the whole run, so the instances before today read them"
  etf_seen = 100 governs 2024-01-01..2024-06-30 "01-month.json price.etf, syntetyczne"
  etf_seen = 108 governs 2024-07-01..2024-12-31 "price.etf, syntetyczne"
  etf_seen = 113 governs 2025-01-01..2025-06-30 "price.etf, syntetyczne"
  etf_seen = 110 governs 2025-07-01..2025-12-31 "price.etf, syntetyczne"
  etf_seen = 121 governs 2026-01-01..2026-06-30 "price.etf, syntetyczne"
  etf_seen = 126 governs 2026-07-01.. "price.etf, syntetyczne, the last entry before the assumed growth"
  etf_from = 2026-11 "price.etf grows each month from 2026-11-01"
  units_step = 0.000000000001 "the prototype keeps units as floats; here to 1e-12 of a unit"
  etf_price_step = 0.000000000001 "the prototype keeps price.etf as a float; here each month's price to 1e-12 zł"
  invest_dom = 15 "02-rule-15.json: on the 15th of each month"
  invest_from = 2026-11 "run.ts runs a rule's line from today (2026-10-17) on: the first 15th is 2026-11-15"
  floor_15 = 1000 "02-rule-15.json, 03-ike-first.json: floor 1 000"
  oki_from = 2027-01 "07-oki.json: invest_15 until 2027-01-01, invest_15_oki and oki_tax from 2027-01-01"
  fire_rate = 0.04 "13-fire.json assume.fire_swr: 4 %"
  fire_from = 2026-10 "fire@1 kiedy: first('on_track') over the line's months from today's (run.ts answers: evalDate >= today)"

version ike_limits
  cite ike_act
  governs always
  known 2025-12-31
  ike_limit = 23472 governs 2024-01-01..2024-12-31 "03-ike-first.json ike.limit: 3 × 7 824 zł"
  ike_limit = 26019 governs 2025-01-01..2025-12-31 "3 × 8 673 zł"
  ike_limit = 28260 governs 2026-01-01.. "3 × 9 420 zł (M.P. 2025 poz. 1206); the prototype holds it past its last entry (law held after today)"

version nbp_2026_03
  cite rpp
  governs 2026-03-05..
  known 2026-03-04
  nbp_ref = 0.0375 "07-oki.json nbp.ref_rate: RPP, decyzja z 4.03.2026, utrzymana 6–7.10.2026; held past its last entry"

version oki_2027
  cite oki_act
  governs always
  known 2026-07-15
  oki_rate_first = 0.0085 "art. 43: the first year's rate"
  oki_ref_from = 2028-01-01 "art. 25: from 2028, the rate follows the NBP reference rate"
  oki_ref_share = 0.19 "art. 25: 19 % of the NBP reference rate"
  oki_rate_step = 0.0001 "art. 25: down to 0.01 pp"
  oki_rate_floor = 0.001 "art. 25: at least 0.1 %"
  oki_exempt = 0 "art. 26: holds foreign (oki_tax holds: foreign): no exempt amount"
  oki_tax_month = 5 "oki_pl@2027 tax: next_year:05-31, bd next"
  oki_tax_day = 31 "next_year:05-31"
  nbp_months = 2 "art. 25: the rate of 31 October, two months before the year's 31 December"
,17:r7/business.tally,7582:part r7_business
  tally 2
  note "T, M2 (issues #167, #114): the side business of R7 (05-side-business.json: dzialalnosc@1 from 2026-03-01, revenue 6 000 a month, costs 400 with 92 of VAT; jdg_pl@2026 form ryczalt, zus_stage zbieg, no sickness; vat_pl@2026), every line with its movement on konto, as M1's restatement (m1/goldens/business/model.tally) gives its 2026 pins. The lines follow the prototype's template: the health of the month by the revenue from the year's start (ytd), the advance on the year's running base less half the year's health, settled with the year's return; the year's health settled in May; VAT on the 25th. Days: revenue and its VAT next_month:10, costs day:15, health and the advance next_month:20 bd next, VAT next_month:25 bd next, the settlements next_year:04-30 and 05-20 bd next."
  note "Not stated: the social contributions, 0 every month in concurrence (zbieg: base 0, so zus.pay is 0 and books nothing); the car lines, 0. The ryczałt health wage is held past its last entry (9 228.64 from 2026), as the prototype holds it."

source prototype_biz "the prototype's block 05-side-business.json and its templates dzialalnosc@1, jdg_pl@2026, vat_pl@2026 (engine/spec/verification/blocks)"

kind fee_pays: event certain
  leg net: PLN
  leg vat: PLN

index tier = [low, mid, high]

input biz_from: month

input cost_dom: int

input cost_net: money PLN

input cost_vat: money PLN

input fee_dom: int

input fee_net: money PLN

input health_settle_day: int

input health_settle_month: int

input health_share[t in tier]: num

input pit_settle_day: int

input pit_settle_month: int

input ryczalt_health_ded: num

input ryczalt_rate: num

input ryczalt_wage: money PLN

input vat_dom: int

input vat_rate: num

input zus_dom: int

band health_tier(rev: num PLN): key tier
  note "health.ryczalt_tiers: the band of the year's revenue less social contributions (band: the last row whose from is below)"

def rev_ytd[m in month]: money PLN = sum(fee_net for k in month where year_of(k) == year_of(m) and k >= biz_from and k <= m) at start_of(m)
  note "ytd('revenue', in.business) - ytd('zus.social'), the social contributions 0"

def biz_health[m in month]: money PLN = round(round(ryczalt_wage * health_share[health_tier(rev_ytd[m])], minor(PLN), half-up) * health_rate, minor(PLN), half-up) at start_of(m)
  note "jdg_pl@2026 health, ryczalt: grosze(grosze(p.health.ryczalt_wage * band(tiers, ytd revenue - ytd social)) * p.health.rate)"

def biz_health_ytd[m in month]: money PLN = sum(biz_health[k] for k in month where year_of(k) == year_of(m) and k >= biz_from and k <= m) at start_of(m)

def biz_tax_ytd[m in month]: num PLN = ryczalt_rate * round(max(0, rev_ytd[m] - ryczalt_health_ded * biz_health_ytd[m]), 1, half-up) at start_of(m)
  note "tax.base zl(max(0, ytd revenue - ytd social - p.pit.ryczalt_health_share * ytd health)); tax.ytd in.ryczalt_rate * tax.base"

def biz_adv[m in month]: money PLN = max(0, round(biz_tax_ytd[m], 1, half-up) - sum(biz_adv[k] for k in month where year_of(k) == year_of(m) and k >= biz_from and k < m)) at start_of(m)
  note "pit.advance: max(0, zl(v('tax.ytd')) - ytd_before('pit.advance'))"

def biz_months[y in cal_year]: int = count(k in month where year_of(k) == y and k >= biz_from) at start_of(y)

def biz_pit_settle[y in cal_year]: money PLN = round(biz_tax_ytd[month_of(add_days(end_of(y), -1))], 1, half-up) - sum(biz_adv[k] for k in month where year_of(k) == y and k >= biz_from) at start_of(y)
  note "pit.settle: zl(last('tax.ytd')) - total('pit.advance')"

def biz_health_settle[y in cal_year]: money PLN = biz_months[y] * round(round(ryczalt_wage * health_share[health_tier(rev_ytd[month_of(add_days(end_of(y), -1))])], minor(PLN), half-up) * health_rate, minor(PLN), half-up) - sum(biz_health[k] for k in month where year_of(k) == y and k >= biz_from) at start_of(y)
  note "health.settle: total('active') * grosze(grosze(p.health.ryczalt_wage * band(tiers, total revenue - total social)) * p.health.rate) - total('health')"

def biz_vat[m in month]: money PLN = round(fee_net * vat_rate, minor(PLN), half-up) - cost_vat at start_of(m)
  note "vat.due: v('vat.out') - v('vat.in'), vat.out grosze(revenue * p.vat.rate)"

move biz_fee[m in month]: fee_pays
  on add_months(day_of(m, fee_dom), 1)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  when m >= biz_from
  leg net from klienci to konto amount fee_net
  leg vat from klienci to konto amount round(fee_net * vat_rate, minor(PLN), half-up)

move biz_costs[m in month]: transfers
  on day_of(m, cost_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  when m >= biz_from
  leg cash from konto to dostawcy amount cost_net + cost_vat

move biz_health_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(start_of(m), 1)), zus_dom, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  when m >= biz_from
  leg cash from konto to zus amount biz_health[m]

move biz_adv_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(start_of(m), 1)), zus_dom, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  when m >= biz_from
  leg cash from konto to urzad_skarbowy amount biz_adv[m]

move biz_vat_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(start_of(m), 1)), vat_dom, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  when m >= biz_from
  leg cash from konto to urzad_skarbowy amount biz_vat[m]

move biz_pit_settle_pay[y in cal_year]: settles
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(add_years(start_of(y), 1), pit_settle_month - 1)), pit_settle_day, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(y)
  for y
  when end_of(y) > start_of(biz_from)
  leg pay from konto to urzad_skarbowy amount max(0, biz_pit_settle[y])
  leg refund from urzad_skarbowy to konto amount max(0, -biz_pit_settle[y])

move biz_health_settle_pay[y in cal_year]: settles
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(add_years(start_of(y), 1), health_settle_month - 1)), health_settle_day, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(y)
  for y
  when end_of(y) > start_of(biz_from)
  leg pay from konto to zus amount max(0, biz_health_settle[y])
  leg refund from zus to konto amount max(0, -biz_health_settle[y])

version business_2026
  cite prototype_biz
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  note "stated for the whole run, as the prototype's fixture is one model with one today; the business itself starts 2026-03-01"
  biz_from = 2026-03 "05-side-business.json: business from 2026-03-01"
  fee_net = 6000 "dzialalnosc@1: revenue 6 000 a month"
  cost_net = 400 "dzialalnosc@1: costs 400"
  cost_vat = 92 "dzialalnosc@1: costs_vat 92"
  fee_dom = 10 "revenue.cash, vat.out: next_month:10"
  cost_dom = 15 "costs.cash: day:15"
  zus_dom = 20 "health.pay, pit.advance: next_month:20, bd next"
  vat_dom = 25 "vat.due: next_month:25, bd next"
  pit_settle_month = 4 "pit.settle: next_year:04-30, bd next"
  pit_settle_day = 30 "next_year:04-30"
  health_settle_month = 5 "health.settle: next_year:05-20, bd next"
  health_settle_day = 20 "next_year:05-20"
  ryczalt_rate = 0.12 "jdg_pl@2026 ryczalt_rate, 12 %"
  ryczalt_health_ded = 0.5 "pit.ryczalt_health_share: ustawa o ryczałcie art. 11 ust. 1a"
  ryczalt_wage = 9228.64 "health.ryczalt_wage from 2026: GUS, IV kw. 2025, M.P. 2026 poz. 117; held after"
  health_share[low] = 0.6 "health.ryczalt_tiers: ustawa o świadczeniach art. 81 ust. 2h"
  health_share[mid] = 1 "art. 81 ust. 2h"
  health_share[high] = 1.8 "art. 81 ust. 2h"
  health_tier: [0, 60000] = low "art. 81 ust. 2h: to 60 000"
  health_tier: (60000, 300000] = mid "art. 81 ust. 2h: to 300 000"
  health_tier: (300000, inf) = high "art. 81 ust. 2h: above 300 000"
  vat_rate = 0.23 "vat.rate"
,14:r7/joint.tally,2563:part r7_returns_joint
  tally 2
  note "T, M2 (issues #167, #114): the twin of returns.tally, the prototype's own joint return (04-employment.json pit_joint: pit_return@2022 with a = my_tax, b = wife_tax), which L-26 (art. 6 ust. 8 PIT) bars beside the ryczałt of 05-side-business. Read in place of returns.tally, it shows that L-26 alone moves the pins it moves: on this twin R7 prints the prototype's figures. tax = zl(2 * max(0, brackets(p.pit.scale, (base_a + base_b) / 2) - p.pit.reduction)), due = tax - both spouses' advances, filed under my name (my_job's row; wife_job's 0)."

source prototype_ret "the prototype's block 04-employment.json, template pit_return@2022 (engine/spec/verification/blocks)"

kind settles: event certain
  leg pay: PLN
  leg refund: PLN

input joint_halves: int

input return_day: int

input return_month: int

def pit_income[j in job, y in cal_year]: num PLN = sum(gross[j, m] - kup_month - emp_zus[j, m] for m in month where year_of(m) == y) at start_of(y)
  note "employment_pl@2022 income: gross - costs of earning - social contributions, summed over the year"

def pit_base[j in job, y in cal_year]: money PLN = round(max(0, pit_income[j, y]), 1, half-up) at start_of(y)
  note "pit_return@2022 base_a, base_b: zl(max(0, year_sum(income)))"

def pit_adv_year[y in cal_year]: money PLN = sum(emp_pit_adv[my_job, m] + emp_pit_adv[wife_job, m] for m in month where year_of(m) == y) at start_of(y)
  note "pit_return@2022 advances: year_sum(a, pit.advance) + year_sum(b, pit.advance)"

def pit_due[j in job, y in cal_year]: money PLN at start_of(y)
  note "pit_return@2022 due: v('tax') - v('advances'), the joint return's tax on half the two bases, twice; pit_scale already takes the reducing amount off"
  rule joint = round(joint_halves * max(0, pit_scale((pit_base[my_job, y] + pit_base[wife_job, y]) / joint_halves)), 1, half-up) - pit_adv_year[y] when j == my_job
  rule spouse beats joint = 0 when j == wife_job

move pit_return[y in cal_year, j in job on end_of(y)]: settles
  on schedule(month_of(add_months(add_years(start_of(y), 1), return_month - 1)), return_day, following, holidays_pl)
  at start_of(y)
  for y
  leg pay from konto to urzad_skarbowy amount max(0, pit_due[j, y])
  leg refund from urzad_skarbowy to konto amount max(0, -pit_due[j, y])

version returns_2022
  cite prototype_ret
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  joint_halves = 2 "pit_return@2022 tax: twice the tax on half the joint base"
  return_month = 4 "pit_return@2022 due: next_year:04-30, bd next"
  return_day = 30 "next_year:04-30"
